":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1507.375,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":106.75,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":24585.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1309.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an Approach section that DECIDES the fix mechanism: whether the bound uses a wall-clock `timeout=`, the `stall_abort_args()` splice, or both, and HOW stderr is drained concurrently while stdout streams into tarfile.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Prefer splicing that for any network-reaching git call over only shortening a wall clock' — a preference, not a decision","'Route it through this module's error conversion' — names a seam but not the concrete call change","No section describes HOW stderr gets drained (concurrent thread? communicate()? tempfile?) while stdout is streamed into tarfile"],"finding":"The plan states the three defects and desired outcomes but never decides the fix MECHANISM: the Constraints section says to 'Prefer splicing [stall_abort_args] for any network-reaching git call over only shortening a wall clock' and to 'Route [TimeoutExpired] through this module's error conversion', yet no Approach/Fix section commits to whether the bound is a wall-clock timeout=, the stall_abort_args splice, or both, nor how stderr will be drained concurrently.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1fdd010ca9fcb546","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan body (no 'Approach'/'Fix' section; Constraints section)","norm_id":"n759ecd8821fd7139","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor picks a bare wall-clock timeout=, satisfying AC2 'bounded' but ignoring the stall_abort_args guidance for the promisor (network-reaching) path","Two executors choose different stderr-draining strategies, one of which reintroduces the deadlock"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State e.g.: 'Splice stall_abort_args() into the archive Popen for the lazy-fetch path, drain stderr on a reader thread (or capture to a tempfile), pass stdin=DEVNULL, and convert TimeoutExpired via this module's error-conversion helper before it escapes.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add/extend an acceptance criterion that verifies the network-reaching archive path is bounded by the stall-based mechanism (stall_abort_args / lowSpeedLimit) rather than only a wall-clock timeout, or explicitly justify why wall-clock is sufficient for `git archive` on a local sha.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3637,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'The subprocess is bounded, and a stalled child is terminated'","Constraint: 'Elapsed time is the wrong axis for a stalled transfer ... Prefer splicing that stall_abort_args() seam ... over only shortening a wall clock'"],"finding":"No acceptance criterion pins whether the network-reaching (promisor lazy-fetch) stall — defect 1, the one with a demonstrated multi-minute block — is bounded via the preferred stall_abort_args seam versus only a wall-clock timeout; AC2 says only 'the subprocess is bounded', which a plain elapsed-time timeout would satisfy while contradicting the Constraints guidance that 'elapsed time is the wrong axis for a stalled transfer'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe8e678baf7f6d4d8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC2) vs Constraints (stall_abort_args paragraph)","norm_id":"nf19ce410d01d765a","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Fix ships a wall-clock timeout only; AC2 passes green but the stated-preferred stall-abort mechanism is absent, and the constraint about elapsed-time-being-wrong is silently violated"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Commit AC line 2 to a specific bounding mechanism for the promisor stall (throughput-keyed stall_abort_args() vs elapsed-time timeout) and state the positive rationale, reconciling it with the 512 MiB large-archive case.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Prefer splicing that for any network-reaching git call over only shortening a wall clock' — stated as a preference, not committed in any AC","Plan AC2: 'The subprocess is bounded, and a stalled child is terminated rather than left running' — does not name timeout vs stall-abort","git_fetch.py:169 'bounds ELAPSED TIME, which is the wrong axis for a stalled transfer'; snapshot.py:43 DEFAULT_MAX_SNAPSHOT_BYTES=512 MiB means a plain timeout risks killing a legitimately large archive"],"finding":"The plan does not commit to (or state a positive rationale for) which mechanism bounds defect 1's promisor stall: an elapsed-time communicate(timeout=) versus splicing git_fetch.stall_abort_args(). The plan's own Constraints section, citing suave-constant-cow and git_fetch.py:169, argues elapsed time is the WRONG axis for a stalled transfer, yet AC line 2 ('The subprocess is bounded... a stalled child is terminated') is mechanism-agnostic and would be satisfiable by a plain wall-clock timeout that the constraint warns against and that would also abort a healthy-but-large archive (a 512 MiB / 200k-file cap exists in snapshot.py). Pick and justify the mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ee19059f9f14edd","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 2 + 'Constraints on the fix' section","norm_id":"n043e2736918bf2d5","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A large-but-healthy repo whose git archive legitimately exceeds a fixed wall-clock timeout gets its snap